course: dictionary
lesson: 12803
title: Elevation: height and rank
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Elevation is a noun, a thing you can name. Its most common meaning is height: how high a place is above sea level. «The village is at an elevation of 500 metres.» This means the village sits 500 metres above the sea.
explain: Look at the clue words around it. Words like «above sea level», «metres» and «high» tell you that elevation is about height. Try the swap check: «The village is at a height of 500 metres above sea level» still makes sense, so elevation means height here.
explain: Elevation can also mean raising something or someone up, or moving them to a higher rank. «Her elevation to captain made the whole team cheer.» No mountain is involved here. She was moved to a higher position, and the context shows which meaning the writer means.
explain: In geography, maps show elevation with colours and contour lines. In maths, you can subtract two elevations to find how much higher one place is. Architects also use elevation for a flat drawing of one side of a building, but that is a technical meaning.
fact: Elevation means the height of a place above sea level.
fact: «High elevation» means a place that is a long way above sea level, such as a mountain top.
fact: Elevation can also mean raising something or someone up, or moving them to a higher rank.
fact: On a map, colours and contour lines show elevation.
fact: Useful phrases: «at an elevation of» and «elevation above sea level».
exercise: «The hikers reached a high elevation before lunch.» What does elevation mean here? | A flat drawing of a house | Raising a flag up a pole | *Height above sea level | A deep valley
exercise: «Her elevation to captain made the whole team cheer.» What does elevation mean here? | Being at the bottom of a hill | Feeling very tired | *Moving someone to a higher rank | A flat drawing of a building
exercise: «The town is at an elevation of 300 metres.» Which word in the sentence tells you elevation is about height? | town | *metres | team | cheer
test: «The farm is at an elevation of 200 metres.» What is the elevation of the farm? | How many animals it has | *Its height above sea level | How far it is from the school | Its colour on a map
test: «The architect drew the elevation of the new school.» What is an elevation here? | *A flat drawing of one side of the building | A school trip up a mountain | A kind of paint | A tall tower on a hill
exam: «The climbers reached an elevation of 3000 metres, so the air felt thin.» What does elevation mean in this sentence? | Moving someone to a higher rank | A type of climbing rope | *Height above sea level | A flat drawing of one side of a building
